From: Wine upstream contributors (see commit list)
Subject: [PATCH] Backport targeted Wine 11.19 fixes.

Squashed backport of 87 WineHQ commits first released in wine-11.19, applied in upstream
order on top of cx26.3-wine11.0-runeon.15 patches 0001-0110. Test-only hunks are omitted.
Adaptations, marked [adapted] below: 60551e1d7b places the overflow checks before both
aligned allocations, because the base lacks a later shrink-padding block; 105ced5bc1 is the
same one-line change with different surrounding lines; 53b5345251 and 37fd158bfc are combined
so that Flush resets only an active renderer that still has an audio client, as the base has no
position/pts fields; ee38ff1725 compares with ~(DWORD)0 because the base lacks intsafe.h.

  38e3dc2e53 Alistair Leslie-Hughes: windows.devices.enumeration: Return E_NOINTERFACE when no interface found.
  01599743e2 Tobiasz Laskowski: ole32: Fix DoDragDrop uninitialized error code.
  3c5e9cf70d Alex Henrie: comctl32: Check array length before dereferencing in TOOLBAR_WrapToolbar.
  6a1df4121c Alex Henrie: shell32: Allocate enough space for the final null in build_paths_list.
  b47d5ddb5c Alex Henrie: crypt32: Pass the correct length when querying CNGExtraAlgid.
  105ced5bc1 Alex Henrie: msvcrt: Pass buffer size in WCHARs from _wassert to _snwprintf. [adapted]
